WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.090
Question eighteen. Highlight: the same clip on a phone and a larger T V still looks detailed — mainly because?

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:13.459
Useful: clear across screen sizes → higher pixel resolution keeps detail.

00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:16.548
Useless: phone or T V brand — not the key.

00:00:16.548 --> 00:00:20.446
Option A. Lower bit rate: usually hurts detail — cut.

00:00:20.446 --> 00:00:25.153
Option B. Fewer audio tracks: unrelated to picture detail — cut.

00:00:25.153 --> 00:00:29.271
Option C. Smaller file: does not guarantee detail — cut.

00:00:29.271 --> 00:00:32.286
Option D. Higher pixel resolution — keep.

00:00:32.286 --> 00:00:36.331
Detail stays clear mainly from higher pixel resolution.

00:00:36.331 --> 00:00:38.832
Therefore the correct answer is D.
